---
title: A4 — MCP 2026-07-28 | authorised discovery, invocation and denial
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Business user
  participant H as Enterprise host
  participant C as MCP client
  participant I as Identity provider
  participant G as Unity Gateway
  participant P as SWDA policy authority
  participant S as Private MCP server
  participant A as Recommendation agent
  participant T as Classification tool
  participant L as Catalogue lookup
  participant D as Curated catalogue
  participant O as Audit / monitoring

  U->>H: Submit recommendation request
  H->>I: Authenticate user and obtain dedicated host OAuth M2M token
  I-->>H: User session and scoped host service-principal token
  H->>C: Host-authorised request and service-principal token
  Note over C,G: Target revision 2026-07-28 uses self-describing requests. Verify interoperability.
  opt Optional capability discovery, if target protocol supported
    C->>G: server/discover + request metadata
    G->>G: Validate host token and service discovery permission
    G-->>C: Permitted capabilities or controlled denial
  end
  C->>G: tools/list + authenticated host principal
  G->>G: Validate host token, UC EXECUTE grants and tool selectors
  G->>S: Request permitted tool catalogue via managed proxy
  S->>P: Check published manifest, digest, expiry and policy freshness
  alt Discovery approved
    P-->>S: Active scoped tool allowlist
    S-->>G: Permitted server tools
    G-->>C: Filtered tools/list (cache hints if supported)
  else Not approved / revoked / policy unavailable
    P-->>S: Deny, no valid approval
    S-->>G: Denied or empty catalogue
    G-->>C: Controlled discovery denial
  end

  C->>G: tools/call recommend_service (structured input)
  G->>G: Recheck host identity, UC grants and selected tool
  alt Gateway rejects caller or tool
    G-->>C: Access denied / unavailable (no backend invocation)
  else Gateway allows
    G->>S: Managed proxy, authenticated backend service identity
    S->>P: Fresh call-time policy: exact deployed digest, status, tool, scope, expiry
    alt Revoked, expired, stale or registry unreachable
      P-->>S: DENY (fail closed)
      S-->>G: Sanitised policy denial
      G-->>C: Controlled denial
    else Active approval and matching release
      P-->>S: Allow with restricted service scope
      S->>S: Validate protocol version, headers, input schema / limits
      alt Invalid input, protocol or policy
        S-->>G: Sanitised validation error
        G-->>C: Controlled error
      else Valid request
        S->>A: Execute service recommendation
        A->>T: Deterministic classification
        T-->>A: Class and rule reference
        A->>L: Approved catalogue lookup
        L->>D: Read-only filtered records
        D-->>L: Minimal programme facts + catalogue version
        L-->>A: Eligible programme matches
        A-->>S: Structured result + provenance
        S->>S: Validate output schema / redaction
        S-->>G: Validated MCP tool result or safe tool error
        G-->>C: Result / controlled failure
        C-->>H: Parsed, validated response
        H-->>U: Recommendation or safe failure
      end
    end
  end
  G-->>O: UC audit and usage events, trace ID / status
  S-->>O: SWDA decision / invocation events, no secrets or raw sensitive payload
  Note over G,S: No public backend ingress. SWDA checks do not depend on unverified Gateway policy hooks.
  Note over H,S: Host enforces user permissions. Backend sees service identity only without verified delegation.
